    "explanation": "(a) $E = m\\left(gh + \\frac{1}{2}v^2\\right)$. (b) $m = \\frac{E}{gh + \\frac{1}{2}v^2} = \\frac{2E}{2gh + v^2}$. (c) $m = \\frac{3000}{240 + 36} = \\frac{3000}{276} = 10.869\\ldots \\approx 10.9$ kg. (d) $\\frac{1}{2}mv^2 = E - mgh$, so $v = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(E - mgh)}{m}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 300}{10}} = \\sqrt{60} = 7.745\\ldots \\approx 7.75$ m/s.",
    "workedSolution": "**(a)** Take out $m$: $m\\left(gh + \\frac{1}{2}v^2\\right)$.\n\n**(b)** Divide by the bracket: $m = \\frac{E}{gh + \\frac{1}{2}v^2}$ **(M1)**; $= \\frac{2E}{2gh + v^2}$ **(A1)**.\n\n**(c)** $\\frac{2 \\times 1500}{2 \\times 10 \\times 12 + 6^2} = \\frac{3000}{276}$ **(M1)** $= 10.9$ **(A1)**.\n\n**(d)** $5v^2 = 1500 - 1200 = 300$ **(M1)**, so $v^2 = 60$ and $v = 7.75$ **(A1)**.",
